  <!-- OVERVIEW -->
  <section class="section" id="overview">
    <span class="section-label">Progression &amp; Rewards</span>
    <h2>Gamification System</h2>
    <p>VibeCrew includes a persistent progression layer that motivates across sessions and teaches vibe-coding skills over time. It tracks your growth from your first <code>/setup</code> through hundreds of shipped features.</p>

    <div class="principles">
      <div class="principle">
        <div class="principle-icon">&#9878;</div>
        <div>
          <strong>Artifacts over actions</strong>
          <p>Rewards map to real outputs &mdash; shipped features, passing tests, clean sessions &mdash; not arbitrary clicks.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="principle">
        <div class="principle-icon">&#9733;</div>
        <div>
          <strong>Teaching over tracking</strong>
          <p>Every mechanic helps you improve. Challenges target your weakest skills. Quizzes explain the answer.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="principle">
        <div class="principle-icon">&#9829;</div>
        <div>
          <strong>Sustainable over addictive</strong>
          <p>Grace periods for streaks, opt-in challenges, no toxic leaderboards. Taking time off is never punished.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <Callout type="info" title="How it runs">
      <p>The gamification pipeline runs automatically at the end of every <code>/wrap</code>. Six scripts execute sequentially: award XP, check level-up, update streak, distribute skill XP, check badges, and update challenges. You never need to run anything manually.</p>
    </Callout>
  </section>

  <hr>

  <!-- ENABLE / DISABLE -->
  <section class="section" id="enable-disable">
    <span class="section-label">Configuration</span>
    <h2>Enabling &amp; Disabling</h2>
    <p>There are two ways to control gamification, and they stay in sync automatically.</p>

    <h3>Option 1: User Profile (recommended)</h3>
    <p>Run <code>/profile</code> and answer the gamification question. This sets the <code>gamification_preference</code> dimension, and VibeCrew automatically syncs the corresponding config flags.</p>

    <TableWrap>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Profile Setting</th><th>What You See</th><th>Config Flags</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><span class="badge green">All In</span> (<code>full</code>)</td>
            <td>XP, badges, streaks, challenges, level-ups, streak reminders, quizzes &mdash; everything</td>
            <td><code>enabled: true</code>, <code>show_xp: true</code>, <code>streak_reminders: true</code></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><span class="badge blue">Light Touch</span> (<code>light</code>)</td>
            <td>XP and badges display, but no streak reminders &mdash; low-key progression</td>
            <td><code>enabled: true</code>, <code>show_xp: true</code>, <code>streak_reminders: false</code></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><span class="badge amber">Score Only</span> (<code>score_only</code>)</td>
            <td>Vibe Score only. No XP, no badges, no streaks display. Progression still tracked silently</td>
            <td><code>enabled: true</code>, <code>show_xp: false</code>, <code>streak_reminders: false</code></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><span class="badge muted">Disabled</span> (<code>disabled</code>)</td>
            <td>All gamification output suppressed. Vibe Score and Performance Coach still operate independently</td>
            <td><code>enabled: false</code>, <code>show_xp: false</code>, <code>streak_reminders: false</code></td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </TableWrap>

    <h3>Option 2: Direct config edit</h3>
    <p>Edit <code>.vibecrew/config.json</code> directly. The gamification block controls everything:</p>

    <h4>Full gamification (all features on)</h4>
    <CodeBlock code={configFull} lang="json" />

    <h4>Gamification disabled</h4>
    <CodeBlock code={configDisabled} lang="json" />

    <Callout type="tip" title="What happens when disabled?">
      <p>All gamification scripts check <code>config.json</code> on entry. When <code>enabled</code> is <code>false</code>, every script exits immediately with no output and no file modifications. Your <code>gamification.json</code> data is preserved &mdash; nothing is deleted. Re-enable at any time and pick up where you left off.</p>
    </Callout>

    <Callout type="warn" title="Vibe Score is independent">
      <p>Disabling gamification does <strong>not</strong> disable the Vibe Score. The score measures session quality and feeds the Performance Coach &mdash; it operates as a core system, not a gamification feature. You always get your score at <code>/wrap</code>.</p>
    </Callout>
  </section>

  <hr>

  <!-- VIBE SCORE -->
  <section class="section" id="vibe-score">
    <span class="section-label">Session Quality</span>
    <h2>Vibe Score</h2>
    <p>Every session ends with a quality score (0&ndash;130+). It starts at 100 and adjusts based on real work artifacts. The score is the single data source for XP, badges, challenges, and Performance Coach analysis.</p>

    <h3>Deductions</h3>
    <p>Points are removed for anti-patterns detected during the session:</p>

    <TableWrap>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Anti-Pattern</th><th>Deduction</th><th>What It Means</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Prompt churn</td><td>&minus;5 per sequence</td><td>Rephrasing the same instruction multiple times without progress</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Tool loops</td><td>&minus;10 per loop</td><td>Retrying the same failed command with the same approach</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Low cache utilization</td><td>&minus;15</td><td>Cache ratio below 50% (inefficient token usage)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Context violations</td><td>&minus;20</td><td>Peak context usage exceeded 60% of the window</td></tr>
          <tr><td>No tests</td><td>&minus;10</td><td>Test files exist but zero tests pass</td></tr>
          <tr><td>No feature spec</td><td>&minus;5</td><td>Active feature missing acceptance criteria</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Skipped code review</td><td>&minus;5</td><td>Review phase not completed for the feature</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Documentation drift</td><td>&minus;3 per stale doc</td><td>Source code changed but matching feature docs not updated</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Console errors</td><td>&minus;5</td><td>Console errors detected on affected pages</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Visual token violations</td><td>&minus;3 each (max &minus;9)</td><td>Design system token violations (hardcoded colors, wrong spacing, etc.)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Plan revisions &ge; 2</td><td>&minus;5</td><td>Plan or spec revised 2+ times mid-feature (insufficient upfront planning)</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </TableWrap>

    <Callout type="info" title="Phase artifact expectations">
      <p>Expected artifacts per phase: Plan &rarr; <code>docs/features/{name}/plan.md</code>, Design &rarr; <code>design.md</code>, Code &rarr; source files, Test &rarr; test files, Docs &rarr; feature documentation. Trivial features skip Design and Review, so missing <code>design.md</code> or review reports are not penalized for trivial complexity.</p>
    </Callout>

    <h3>Bonuses</h3>
    <p>Points are awarded for best practices:</p>

    <TableWrap>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Best Practice</th><th>Bonus</th><th>Condition</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Complete phase artifacts</td><td>+30 max</td><td>All Tier 2 phases (Plan, UI, Code, Test, Review, Docs) completed</td></tr>
          <tr><td>High cache utilization</td><td>+10</td><td>Cache ratio above 70%</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Full test coverage</td><td>+15</td><td>Coverage above 80%</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Clean session</td><td>+5</td><td>Zero deductions</td></tr>
          <tr><td>TDD discipline</td><td>+3</td><td>Tests written before implementation code</td></tr>
          <tr><td>E2E tests passing</td><td>+3</td><td>Playwright/E2E suite passes</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Accessibility clean</td><td>+2</td><td>No critical or serious a11y issues</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Code review complete</td><td>+2</td><td>Review phase completed for the feature</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Performance baselines</td><td>+2</td><td>Performance metrics tracked</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Visual compliance clean</td><td>+3</td><td>Design system tokens used correctly throughout</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </TableWrap>

    <Callout type="tip" title="A perfect session">
      <p>A session with zero deductions and all bonuses can score 130+. This is rare but achievable &mdash; it means you planned thoroughly, wrote tests first, hit high cache, shipped with docs, and kept the context window lean.</p>
    </Callout>
  </section>

  <hr>

  <!-- XP & LEVELING -->
  <section class="section" id="xp-leveling">
    <span class="section-label">Progression</span>
    <h2>XP &amp; Leveling</h2>
    <p>XP is earned through real development work. Every source maps to existing tracked data &mdash; there are no gamification-only actions to grind.</p>

    <h3>XP sources</h3>
    <TableWrap>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Action</th><th>XP</th><th>Data Source</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Complete a session (<code>/wrap</code>)</td><td>+10 base</td><td>Session log</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Vibe Score bonus</td><td>+(score &minus; 50) if &gt;50</td><td>Score file</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Clean session (0 deductions)</td><td>+25</td><td>Score file</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Complete a Tier 2 phase</td><td>+5 per phase</td><td>Phase tracking</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Ship a feature (all 6 phases)</td><td>+50</td><td>Backlog column</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Complete Tier 1 foundation</td><td>+100 (one-time)</td><td>state.json</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Tests pass on first run</td><td>+15</td><td>Test results</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Quiz correct answer</td><td>+5 per answer</td><td>Quiz event</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Challenge completion</td><td>20&ndash;100 (varies)</td><td>Challenge definition</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </TableWrap>

    <h3>Leveling curve</h3>
    <p>XP per level follows an exponential curve: <code>floor(100 &times; 1.15<sup>(level&minus;1)</sup>)</code>. Early levels come quickly to build momentum. Later levels require sustained consistent work.</p>

    <TableWrap>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Level</th><th>Title</th><th>XP to Next</th><th>Approximate Sessions</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>1</td><td><span class="badge muted">Newcomer</span></td><td>100</td><td>2&ndash;3</td></tr>
          <tr><td>2&ndash;3</td><td><span class="badge muted">Apprentice</span></td><td>115&ndash;132</td><td>4&ndash;6</td></tr>
          <tr><td>4&ndash;5</td><td><span class="badge blue">Focused Builder</span></td><td>152&ndash;175</td><td>8&ndash;10</td></tr>
          <tr><td>6&ndash;8</td><td><span class="badge blue">Efficient Coder</span></td><td>201&ndash;266</td><td>12&ndash;18</td></tr>
          <tr><td>9&ndash;12</td><td><span class="badge purple">Seasoned Viber</span></td><td>306&ndash;404</td><td>20&ndash;30</td></tr>
          <tr><td>13&ndash;18</td><td><span class="badge purple">Workflow Master</span></td><td>465&ndash;808</td><td>35&ndash;55</td></tr>
          <tr><td>19&ndash;25</td><td><span class="badge amber">Context Architect</span></td><td>929&ndash;2,113</td><td>60&ndash;100</td></tr>
          <tr><td>26&ndash;35</td><td><span class="badge amber">Vibe Sensei</span></td><td>2,430&ndash;6,621</td><td>110&ndash;200</td></tr>
          <tr><td>36&ndash;45</td><td><span class="badge red">Grand Master</span></td><td>7,614&ndash;17,531</td><td>220&ndash;400</td></tr>
          <tr><td>46&ndash;50</td><td><span class="badge red">Vibe Legend</span></td><td>20,161&ndash;28,832</td><td>450+</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </TableWrap>

    <h3>Feature unlocks</h3>
    <p>Features are gated by level to prevent overwhelming new users. Core functionality is <strong>never</strong> gated &mdash; only supplemental gamification features.</p>

    <div class="unlock-timeline">
      <div class="unlock-item">
        <div class="unlock-level">1</div>
        <div class="unlock-content">
          <strong>Base VibeCrew</strong>
          <p>All core workflow, Vibe Score, Performance Coach</p>
