  <!-- DATA FILES -->
  <section class="section" id="data-files">
    <span class="section-label">Technical Details</span>
    <h2>Data Files &amp; Storage</h2>
    <p>All gamification state is stored locally in your project&rsquo;s <code>.vibecrew/</code> directory. Nothing leaves your machine.</p>

    <TableWrap>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>File</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Updated By</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>.vibecrew/gamification.json</code></td><td>Level, XP, badges, skills, streaks, challenges, quiz progress, stats</td><td><code>award-xp.sh</code>, <code>check-badges.sh</code>, <code>update-streak.sh</code>, etc.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>.vibecrew/config.json</code></td><td>Gamification toggle, streak reminders, quiz frequency, user profile</td><td><code>/profile</code>, manual edit</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>.vibecrew/scores/score-*.json</code></td><td>Per-session Vibe Score breakdown (deductions, metrics, phases)</td><td><code>calculate-vibe-score.sh</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>MEMORY.md</code></td><td>Performance Coach persistent memory (anti-patterns, mutations, trends)</td><td>Performance Coach agent</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>.vibecrew/mutation-log.json</code></td><td>History of proposed, accepted, and rejected CLAUDE.md mutations</td><td><code>apply-mutation.sh</code></td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </TableWrap>

    <h3>Concurrency safety</h3>
    <p>All gamification scripts use advisory locks (<code>.vibecrew/locks/gamification.lock</code>) and atomic writes (temp file + mv) to prevent corruption when multiple agents update simultaneously.</p>

    <Callout type="info" title="Data portability">
      <p>Your <code>gamification.json</code> file is self-contained. If you move to a new machine, copy <code>.vibecrew/gamification.json</code> and <code>.vibecrew/config.json</code> to preserve your full progression history.</p>
    </Callout>
  </section>

